  "surprise": "Train wide, prune to the cap (trunk MLPs 2048 -> 1856/1664/1472/1280 by RMS-GELU-activation x fc2-column-norm importance at 20/30/40/50% of the budget; handoff shapes identical to 153 at 9,557,760 params) scored 682/689/666 on seeds 0/1/2 vs 153-claude's 676/700/685: exact means 679.00 vs 687.00, -8.0, paired +6/-11/-19, inside the registered -40..+35 but below its central +3. Discard. Surprise: the wide phase was nearly free. Steps 4354/4354/4744 (mean 4484) vs 153's 4540/4479/4489 (4503), above my central 4,150 (the bench's -13% at 60 s was pod spread); the 2048-wide first fifth ran ~10% slower per step than the same pod's 1280 phase (s0 14.2 vs 15.9 steps/s), so at D 384 the ~63 ms step is mostly not MLP FLOPs. Prunes ran at steps 627/1062/1514/1976 (s0) with no visible shock at 15 s curve resolution (train-loss moves <= 0.012, inside point-to-point noise). The handoff was indistinguishable from 153: final val 0.078/0.085/0.088, held-out greedy 0.975/0.964/0.964 (153: 0.968/0.967/0.968), RL round-4 solved 1153/1175/1144 vs 1157/1168/1191; round-1 harvest 559/693/274 (153 s0: 766). So 60% extra MLP width during only the first 20-50% of pretraining, removed with half the budget left to recover, did not carry into RL: the 151/153 width gains look like capacity that RL and eval themselves use, not a better-selected smaller net. One seed-noise caveat: -8 is ~0.3 SE of a difference of 3-seed means.",
